# REQUIRES: verilator
# The ready-pass search places many choices against a frame found before; a
# paged copy's spacing sets the modulo search's lower bound well under that
# frame (Driver/Inputs/pagewrap: Mid paged off chip, 8 copies, lower bound 16,
# frame 37). Each such choice is tried at the longest period of use first and
# dropped when it does not place there (the premise the search's doubling and
# halving steps rest on); one that places is searched from the lower bound as
# before. The schedule is the one the full search per choice finds (here:
# 1,024 choices placed, 1,238 periods tried in all against 19,801 before),
# and exact against the target. (One fold: no state scratch refold, whose
# search log would count twice.)
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t && cd %S/../Driver/Inputs/pagewrap
# RUN: env FOLDSIM_SEARCH_LOG=1 foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/p --static --modulo --page Mid:1,Leaf:2 --copies Mid:8 --storage Mid:pages=hbm --state-scratch-no-rebuild Mid Leaf > %t/p.log 2>&1
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=REPORT < %t/p/schedule.txt
# RUN: grep -c 'modulo search lower' %t/p.log | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=PLACED
# RUN: %verilator --binary --timing -Wno-fatal -Wno-lint --top-module tb -I%t/p -Mdir %t/p/obj %S/Inputs/tb_pages.sv top.sv %t/p/foldsim_sim.sv > %t/p/build.log 2>&1
# RUN: %t/p/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+0 +verilator+seed+1 +lo=1 +hi=40 +stall=20 +full=10 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %verilator --binary --timing -Wno-fatal -Wno-lint --top-module tb -I%t/p -Mdir %t/p/objm %S/Inputs/tb_pages.sv top_mut.sv %t/p/foldsim_sim.sv > %t/p/buildm.log 2>&1
# RUN: %t/p/objm/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+0 +verilator+seed+1 +lo=1 +hi=1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=MUT
# REPORT: foldsim-fold-static: II = 37
# REPORT-NEXT: modulo search: lower bound 16, 22 periods tried (1238 over the ready-pass search)
# PLACED: 1024
# CHECK-NOT: PROTOCOL
# CHECK: MATCH
# MUT: MISMATCH
